Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that

$$
\begin{aligned}T(kv+w)=T(kv)+T(w)=kT(v)+T(w)\end{aligned}
$$

for any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,

$$
\begin{aligned}T(3{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}) & =3T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2}) \\ [\begin{aligned}-5 \\ 13\end{aligned}] & =3T({v}_{1})+[\begin{aligned}1 \\ 10\end{aligned}] \\ 3T({v}_{1}) & =[\begin{aligned}-5 \\ 13\end{aligned}]-[\begin{aligned}1 \\ 10\end{aligned}] \\ 3T({v}_{1}) & =[\begin{aligned}-6 \\ 3\end{aligned}] \\ T({v}_{1}) & =\frac{1}{3}[\begin{aligned}-6 \\ 3\end{aligned}] \\ T({v}_{1}) & =[\begin{aligned}-2 \\ 1\end{aligned}].\end{aligned}
$$
